 "notes": "ADMX SQUID-amplifier run (812.7-860.3 MHz, i.e. 3.361-3.558 ueV). Curve traced from the vector paths of Fig. 5 (figures/coupling_limits.eps in the e-print): 90% CL excluded g_agamma vs frequency at rho_a=0.45 GeV/cm^3 (paper's assumed density equals the compilation's canonical 0.45, so no rescaling). Of the two scenarios in Fig. 5 the virialized dark-matter model (velocity dispersion 160 km/s, flow 220 km/s) is reported here as the main/standard-halo result; the 'unvirialized' (<=60 km/s dispersion) curve is ~1.5x stronger. The limit is a 28-bin staircase (1.70 MHz bins), emitted as pairs of step-edge points. Axis calibration from decade tick marks, cross-checked: the figure's KSVZ line falls at 1.31e-15 GeV^-1, matching g_agamma(KSVZ) at 3.4 ueV. Text quotes exclusion of realistic axion models over 3.3-3.53 ueV (rounded relative to the plotted 812.7-860.3 MHz scan).",
